    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 10-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate for dual-band operation at 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Stack topology: Air | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Si (10 finite layers, alternating starting with high-index Ta2O5). Initialize all layer thicknesses from iteration_05 best candidate: [56.0, 110.0, 176.0, 172.0, 88.0, 117.0, 111.0, 250.0, 112.0, 45.0] nm. Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with perturbation bounds restricted to ±5 nm per layer per iteration. Thickness constraints: 20-400 nm per layer. Incidence: 0 deg, unpolarized. Objective: minimize weighted mean reflectance across both bands equally, report transmittance into Si. Evaluate candidates by target_score (reflectance minimization), robustness_score, and thicknesses_nm outputs. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
